WEBVTT

00:24:57.849 --> 00:25:00.203
where we all had something
to be happy about again

00:25:00.227 --> 00:25:01.722
and something to celebrate,

00:25:01.746 --> 00:25:05.893
and it was small, but it was a win,
and it brought joy.

00:25:06.825 --> 00:25:09.233
AG: Psychologists have
discovered an alternative

00:25:09.257 --> 00:25:10.782
to post-traumatic stress.

00:25:10.806 --> 00:25:12.689
It's called "post-traumatic growth."

00:25:13.320 --> 00:25:15.696
It's the experience of
not just bouncing back,

00:25:15.720 --> 00:25:17.663
but bouncing forward from adversity.

00:25:18.600 --> 00:25:21.796
Often, it takes the form of
a greater sense of strength.

00:25:21.820 --> 00:25:24.186
CH: This may be the toughest crisis

00:25:24.210 --> 00:25:26.066
any of us have seen in our lifetimes,

00:25:26.090 --> 00:25:28.006
but if we can make it through,

00:25:28.030 --> 00:25:30.286
anything else is a piece of cake.